Grammar

    0 $accept: Program $end

    1 Program: VarDeclList StmtList

    2 VarDeclList: ε
    3            | VarDecl VarDeclList

    4 VarDecl: TYPE ID SEMI
    5        | ARRAY TYPE ID LBRACKET INT_NUMBER RBRACKET SEMI
    6        | TYPE ID

    7 StmtList: ε
    8         | Stmt StmtList

    9 Stmt: ID ASSIGN Expr SEMI
   10     | ID LBRACKET Expr RBRACKET ASSIGN Expr SEMI
   11     | WRITE ID SEMI

   12 Expr: Expr PLUS Expr
   13     | Expr MINUS Expr
   14     | Expr MULTIPLY Expr
   15     | Expr DIVIDE Expr
   16     | ID
   17     | ID LBRACKET Expr RBRACKET
   18     | INT_NUMBER
   19     | FLOAT_NUMBER


Terminals, with rules where they appear

    $end (0) 0
    error (256)
    TYPE <sval> (258) 4 5 6
    ID <sval> (259) 4 5 6 9 10 11 16 17
    SEMI (260) 4 5 9 10 11
    ASSIGN <sval> (261) 9 10
    INT_NUMBER <intVal> (262) 5 18
    FLOAT_NUMBER <floatVal> (263) 19
    WRITE (264) 11
    ARRAY (265) 5
    LBRACKET (266) 5 10 17
    RBRACKET (267) 5 10 17
    PLUS <sval> (268) 12
    MINUS <sval> (269) 13
    MULTIPLY <sval> (270) 14
    DIVIDE <sval> (271) 15


Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

    $accept (17)
        on left: 0
    Program <ast> (18)
        on left: 1
        on right: 0
    VarDeclList <ast> (19)
        on left: 2 3
        on right: 1 3
    VarDecl <ast> (20)
        on left: 4 5 6
        on right: 3
    StmtList <ast> (21)
        on left: 7 8
        on right: 1 8
    Stmt <ast> (22)
        on left: 9 10 11
        on right: 8
    Expr <ast> (23)
        on left: 12 13 14 15 16 17 18 19
        on right: 9 10 12 13 14 15 17


State 0

    0 $accept: • Program $end

    TYPE   shift, and go to state 1
    ARRAY  shift, and go to state 2

    $default  reduce using rule 2 (VarDeclList)

    Program      go to state 3
    VarDeclList  go to state 4
    VarDecl      go to state 5


State 1

    4 VarDecl: TYPE • ID SEMI
    6        | TYPE • ID

    ID  shift, and go to state 6


State 2

    5 VarDecl: ARRAY • TYPE ID LBRACKET INT_NUMBER RBRACKET SEMI

    TYPE  shift, and go to state 7


State 3

    0 $accept: Program • $end

    $end  shift, and go to state 8


State 4

    1 Program: VarDeclList • StmtList

    ID     shift, and go to state 9
    WRITE  shift, and go to state 10

    $default  reduce using rule 7 (StmtList)

    StmtList  go to state 11
    Stmt      go to state 12


State 5

    3 VarDeclList: VarDecl • VarDeclList

